## 2. Inspiration & Historical Accreditation: RVS v0.46 (src/RVS046.tcl)

RVS++ was inspired by and built to preserve computational and autograding parity with **RVS (RISC-V Visual Simulator) v0.46**, originally authored in 2019 by **SIDIC**. 

The inclusion of `src/RVS046.tcl` in this repository serves as the definitive reference implementation and differential testing baseline for RISC-V computer organization coursework. The SIDIC terms below cover **only that file** (`src/RVS046.tcl`); the Rust workspace in `crates/*` is MIT-licensed under section 1. Keep the reference file out of distributions that need to be MIT-only, and treat any reuse of its code (as opposed to its observable behaviour) as governed by SIDIC's not-for-profit terms.

In accordance with the permissions granted in `src/RVS046.tcl` (lines 321–325), the original copyright notice and license terms are reproduced below:

```
***** BETA VERSION FOR EDUCATIONAL USE *****

Copyright (c) 2019. SIDIC. All Rights Reserved.

Permission to use this software for educational not-for-profit purposes without fee
is hereby granted, provided that the above copyright notice, this paragraph and the
following two paragraphs appear in all copies. Contact sidicinfo@yahoo.co.jp for
commercial licensing opportunities.

IN NO EVENT SHALL SIDIC BE LIABLE TO ANY PARTY FOR DIRECT, INDIRECT, SPECIAL,
INCIDENTAL, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES, INCLUDING LOST PROFITS, ARISING OUT OF
THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE AND ITS DOCUMENTATION, EVEN IF SIDIC HAS BEEN ADVISED
OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.

SIDIC SPECIFICALLY DISCLAIMS ANY WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE
IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
THE SOFTWARE AND ACCOMPANYING DOCUMENTATION, IF ANY, PROVIDED HEREUNDER IS
PROVIDED 'AS IS'. SIDIC HAS NO OBLIGATION TO PROVIDE MAINTENANCE, SUPPORT,
UPDATES, ENHANCEMENTS, OR MODIFICATIONS.
